  "silhouette_iou_final_vs_ref": 0.037288977826723434,
  "threshold": 16
}
```

Silhouettes are background-difference masks, not raw brightness thresholds, so
they compare product coverage rather than white background.

## Cloud

The cloud render succeeded at `ubuntu@43.192.32.90:/tmp/mutracer-final/` with
headless Blender `/usr/local/bin/blender` (4.2.23 LTS). The scripts, scene,
asset map, and 436 required assets were uploaded. Asset-map values were remapped
to their keys for the temporary remote layout, and the resulting PNG was pulled
to the path above.

## Gap versus gold

Final framing is restored, but flat white ambient washing removes product
contrast and most product-mask coverage (`brightness_std` 4.97 versus gold
42.81; final-vs-reference IoU 0.037).

